  "text": ".FixedSingle in collection\n.FixedSingle in collection\n.FixedSingle in collection\n\nNo specific mention of community for discussion.\n\nNo specific mention of community for discussion.\nNo mention of attempting to get closer to them.\n\nThat's likely due to the blog post being dedicated only to posts in Vietnamese and English, and the posts that are in these languages are limited to those that mention the community-pioneering target in the title.\n\nTranslate elements to highlight diversity and importance\n\nTranslate the word family to present cultural diversity\nTranslate the word public library to present cultural benefits\nTranslate the word private school to present personal opportunities\nTranslate the word hospital to present medical importance\n\nTranslate elements that emphasize cultural importance and opportunities\n\nTranslate the word fireworks work to present culture\nTranslate the word BLI June 9 to highlight community involvement\nTranslate homework assignment to public notification system\nTranslate month of December on bill to emphasize economic aspects\nTranslate importance of children's lives to legal matters\n\nRemembering the word family will not help foreign speakers add it to the English library and should not be translated into English. 答案\nIn base $b > 5$, if $X > Y$, then the base-$b$ number $\\overline{YXXX}_b$ equals $5b^2 + 2b + 6$. Express $X-Y$ in base $b$.\n\n\\[\n\\overline{YXXX}_b = Y \\times b^3 + X \\times b^2 + X \\times b + X\n\\]\n\nGiven that $\\overline{YXXX}_b = 5b^2 + 2b + 6$, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[\nY \\times b^3 + X \\times b^2 + X \\times b + X = 5b^2 + 2b + 6\n\\]\n\nWe also know that:\n\n\\[\nY < b\n\\]\n\\[\nX > b\n\\]\n\nBy subtracting $5b^2 + 2b + 6$ from both sides of the equation, we aim to express $X-Y$:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nY \\times b^3 & + X \\times b^2 + X \\times b + X - (5b^2 + 2b + 6) \\\\\n&= \\left(5b^2 + 2b + 6\\right) - \\left(5b^2\\right) - \\left(2b\\right) - \\left(6\\right) \\\\\n&= X \\times b^2 + X \\times b\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nHence,\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n(X-Y) \\times b^2 + X \\times b &= 0 \\\\\n\\left[(X-Y)i + b\\right] &= 0\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\nX - Y = 0\n\\]\n\nOr, if considering $X-Y$ as the product, we express it as follows:\n\n\\[\n11b - b = 10b \\implies X - Y = 10b - 10b\n\\]\n\nHence,\n\n\\[\n1 < b\n\\]\n\nGiven that $X > b$, we deduce that $X - Y$ must be a positive value that also appears in the base, concluding that $X - Y = 10 \\times 1 + 6b - 6b = 10$.\n\nTherefore, in base $b$, the value of $X - Y$ is \\boxed{10}.",
